6. External programs invoked as tools (not vendored, not linked)

   LibreOffice / soffice (MPL-2.0) — document-utils conversion, thumbnails
   and formula recalculation.
   Tesseract (Apache-2.0) — optional OCR of scanned pages.
   Node.js (MIT) and a headless Chromium (BSD-3-Clause) — local diagram
   rendering, only after the user consents to a local backend.
   Hugo (Apache-2.0) and the Hugo Book theme (MIT, alex-shpak/hugo-book) —
   optional documentation-site rendering; create-pages fetches the theme
   into the client project at run time, and no theme copy ships here.
   git-delta (MIT) — optional diff viewer for code review.
   git (GPL-2.0) — invoked as a command only.

   Poppler, qpdf and pdftk are NOT required: document-utils renders and
   manipulates PDFs through pypdfium2, pypdf and pdfplumber.

